“You’re catching these characters at a totally different part of their life,&#8221; Brennan told Variety in an interview published Thursday (Nov. 19). &#8220;The timing of these characters thinking, ‘Maybe that was the best time in my life, being in that choir in high school’ and then once you think that you’re like, ‘Oh, that show’s going to work.’”

What&#8217;s more, two core characters are obviously missing, something that would unsurprisingly play a part in the characters&#8217; lives in the reboot. Star Cory Monteith, who portrayed Finn, died at age 31 in July 2013, while the show was between seasons. Glee would go on to pay tribute to the actor in the third episode of season five, which included the character&#8217;s death, though not a cause of death. (Monteith died after mixing alcohol and drugs, according to the B.C. Coroner&#8217;s report at the time.)

Naya Rivera, who played Santana, died in an accidental drowning in July 2020 at age 33, five years after Glee wrapped with its sixth and final season in 2015. The actress died while trying to prevent her son, Josey, from drowning while the two were boating on Lake Piru in California. The little boy, who was 4 at the time, was found safe.

&#8220;We’re still figuring a lot of it out,&#8221; Brennan told Variety of the reboot and two of the stars&#8217; deaths. &#8220;That’s going to be part of it, that sadness and that loss. But still in all, I think [ Glee ] is too big of a thing to sort of let lay. There&#8217;s something about that feels right right now.&#8221;

While the TV producer believes it&#8217;s a good time to bring the show back, he admitted to the publication that he didn&#8217;t always feel that way about a potential reboot. &#8220;I wasn’t that excited about it,&#8221; he said, noting that whenever the topic came up, he&#8217;d wonder why it should even happen. &#8220;For whatever reason, in the last six months or so, I completely did a 180 about it. It just seems the idea is right. I think the time is right. Now I’m really excited about it. It’s going to be a lot of fun.&#8221;

Show creator Ryan Murphy had been teasing a potential reboot this year, even telling Entertainment Tonight in September that he had just finished the script. He shared at the time: “Brad [Falchuk], Ian [Brennan] and I, who wrote all the first two seasons, have written something.&#8221;

After the reboot received a series order by Disney+ and Hulu, reports that certain cast members were already in talks to return began to surface. Among them was Lea Michele , who portrayed Rachel Berry, though her return is not yet officially confirmed. Chris Colfer, who played Kurt Hummel, shared during an interview that he was in talks to return, while Harry Shum Jr. (Mike Chang) — who currently stars as Dr. Kwan on Grey&#8217;s Anatomy — left it a bit vague when he spoke to Entertainment Weekly in late October during his stint on Dancing With the Stars , saying he was &#8220; really, really busy .&#8221; However, the actor added, &#8220;But I would love to keep continuing because I love [ Glee ].&#8221;

Also among the popular Fox show&#8217;s stars — who also landed on Billboard &#8216;s charts collectively as the Glee cast , including an impressive 207 songs on the Billboard Hot 100 — were Jane Lynch as Sue Sylvester, Matthew Morrison as Will Schuester, Kevin McHale as Artie Abrams and Darren Criss as Blaine Anderson.
